The  driver  controls  the cash drawer port of the Protech PS3100
point of sale terminal using the GPIO subsystem.  provides a GPIO
device with two pins: pin 0 is used to control  the  cash  drawer
while  pin  1  can be used to read the current state of the sense
input pin.  A logical 0 means the cash drawer is closed, a  logi‐
cal  1  means  the cash drawer is open.  To open the cash drawer,
set pin 0 to logical 1 for a short period of time (e.g. < 1  sec)
and  then  reset the pin to logical 0.  The driver first appeared
in The driver was written by As it is not possible to detect  the
hardware  at  runtime, this driver, when enabled, will always at‐
tach.  Only enable it in your kernel configuration  if  you  have
the proper hardware.
